Q(14,5,2,"When you back a tractor-trailer, which way do you turn the wheel to make the trailer go left?","To the right",["To the left", "Hold it straight", "It does not matter"],"With a trailer, you turn the steering wheel in the opposite direction. Once the trailer starts to turn, turn the wheel the other way to follow it.");
F(14,5,"When you back a tractor-trailer, which way do you turn the wheel to make the trailer go left?","To the right. With a trailer, you turn the steering wheel in the opposite direction. Once the trailer starts to turn, turn the wheel the other way to follow it.");
Q(14,5,2,"Which trailers are most likely to get stuck on a raised railroad crossing?","Low-slung units such as lowboys, car carriers and moving vans",["Empty flatbeds", "Tankers", "Any trailer under 28 feet"],"Low-slung units and a single-axle tractor pulling a long trailer with landing gear set for a tandem tractor can get stuck.");
F(14,5,"Which trailers are most likely to get stuck on a raised railroad crossing?","Low-slung units such as lowboys, car carriers and moving vans. Low-slung units and a single-axle tractor pulling a long trailer with landing gear set for a tandem tractor can get stuck.");
Q(14,5,2,"If a trailer has no spring brakes, what must you use when parking it?","Wheel chocks",["The trailer hand valve", "The service brake", "Nothing"],"Older trailers without spring brakes will lose their emergency brakes if the air leaks away, so use wheel chocks.");
