Q(14,11,1,"On a tractor-trailer, at what pressure range should the tractor protection valve and parking brake valve pop out?","Between 20 and 45 psi",["Between 60 and 90 psi", "Between 100 and 120 psi", "Only at 0 psi"],"At a range between 20 - 45 psi on a tractor-trailer (or the level specified by the manufacturer), the tractor protection valve and parking brake valve should close (pop out).");
F(14,11,"On a tractor-trailer, at what pressure range should the tractor protection valve and parking brake valve pop out?","Between 20 and 45 psi. At a range between 20 - 45 psi on a tractor-trailer (or the level specified by the manufacturer), the tractor protection valve and parking brake valve should close (pop out).");
Q(14,11,1,"What happens if you do not perform all three parts of the air brake check correctly on the test?","Automatic failure of the vehicle inspection test",["You lose one point", "Nothing, it is optional", "You repeat only that part later"],"Failure to perform all three components of the air brake check correctly results in an automatic failure of the vehicle inspection test.");
F(14,11,"What happens if you do not perform all three parts of the air brake check correctly on the test?","Automatic failure of the vehicle inspection test. Failure to perform all three components of the air brake check correctly results in an automatic failure of the vehicle inspection test.");
Q(14,11,1,"In the hydraulic brake check, what do you do with the brake pedal?","Pump it three times, then hold it down for five seconds; it should not move",["Press it once lightly", "Hold it for one minute while the engine runs", "Pump it twenty times quickly"],"Pump the brake pedal three times, then hold it down for five seconds. The pedal should not move during the five seconds.");
F(14,11,"In the hydraulic brake check, what do you do with the brake pedal?","Pump it three times, then hold it down for five seconds; it should not move. Pump the brake pedal three times, then hold it down for five seconds. The pedal should not move during the five seconds.");
Q(14,11,1,"For the service brake check, at what speed do you pull forward before applying the brake?","5 mph",["15 mph", "25 mph", "1 mph"],"Pull forward at 5 mph, apply the service brake and stop. The vehicle should not pull to either side.");
F(14,11,"For the service brake check, at what speed do you pull forward before applying the brake?","5 mph. Pull forward at 5 mph, apply the service brake and stop. The vehicle should not pull to either side.");
Q(14,11,1,"How must you check tire inflation on the inspection test?","With a tire gauge",["By kicking the tires", "With a mallet", "By looking at them"],"Check for proper inflation with a tire gauge. You get no credit for kicking the tires or using a mallet.");
F(14,11,"How must you check tire inflation on the inspection test?","With a tire gauge. Check for proper inflation with a tire gauge. You get no credit for kicking the tires or using a mallet.");
Q(14,11,1,"What do rust trails or shiny threads around lug nuts show?","Signs of looseness",["New nuts", "Too much torque", "Fresh paint"],"Lug nuts should show no signs of looseness such as rust trails or shiny threads.");
F(14,11,"What do rust trails or shiny threads around lug nuts show?","Signs of looseness. Lug nuts should show no signs of looseness such as rust trails or shiny threads.");
Q(14,11,1,"Which repair is not allowed on rims?","Welding repairs",["Cleaning", "Repainting", "Balancing"],"Check for damaged or bent rims. Rims cannot have welding repairs.");
F(14,11,"Which repair is not allowed on rims?","Welding repairs. Check for damaged or bent rims. Rims cannot have welding repairs.");
Q(14,11,1,"What color must clearance lights be?","Red on the rear, amber elsewhere",["White everywhere", "Blue on the rear", "Green on the sides"],"Clearance lights are red on the rear and amber elsewhere. Reflectors follow the same rule.");
F(14,11,"What color must clearance lights be?","Red on the rear, amber elsewhere. Clearance lights are red on the rear and amber elsewhere. Reflectors follow the same rule.");
Q(14,11,1,"When checking air and electrical lines between tractor and trailer, what must not show through?","Steel braid",["Paint", "Dust", "Labels"],"Air hoses and electrical lines must not be cut, chafed, spliced or worn; steel braid should not show through.");
F(14,11,"When checking air and electrical lines between tractor and trailer, what must not show through?","Steel braid. Air hoses and electrical lines must not be cut, chafed, spliced or worn; steel braid should not show through.");
Q(14,11,1,"How do you check that the parking brake holds?","Gently try to pull forward with the parking brake on",["Rev the engine in neutral", "Roll backward down a hill", "Turn the steering wheel fully"],"With air pressure built up and the parking brake engaged, gently try to pull forward to check that the brake holds the vehicle.");
F(14,11,"How do you check that the parking brake holds?","Gently try to pull forward with the parking brake on. With air pressure built up and the parking brake engaged, gently try to pull forward to check that the brake holds the vehicle.");
Q(14,11,1,"If the vehicle has diesel exhaust fluid (DEF), what level should the tank show?","More than 1/8 of a tank",["Completely empty", "Exactly full only", "Any level is fine"],"Check that the level of diesel exhaust fluid in the DEF tank is adequate (more than 1/8 tank).");
F(14,11,"If the vehicle has diesel exhaust fluid (DEF), what level should the tank show?","More than 1/8 of a tank. Check that the level of diesel exhaust fluid in the DEF tank is adequate (more than 1/8 tank).");
Q(14,8,2,"On doubles and triples, how must the converter dolly air tank drain valve be set before driving?","Closed",["Open", "Half open", "Removed"],"In the walk-around check: shut-off valves at the rear of front trailers open, rear of last trailer closed, and the converter dolly air tank drain valve closed.");
F(14,8,"On doubles and triples, how must the converter dolly air tank drain valve be set before driving?","Closed. In the walk-around check: shut-off valves at the rear of front trailers open, rear of last trailer closed, and the converter dolly air tank drain valve closed.");
Q(14,8,2,"How do you release the brakes on a converter dolly that has no spring brakes?","Open the dolly air tank petcock",["Pull the trailer hand valve", "Disconnect the light cord", "Lower the landing gear"],"Release dolly brakes by opening the air tank petcock, or use the dolly parking brake control if it has spring brakes.");
F(14,8,"How do you release the brakes on a converter dolly that has no spring brakes?","Open the dolly air tank petcock. Release dolly brakes by opening the air tank petcock, or use the dolly parking brake control if it has spring brakes.");
Q(14,8,2,"When you charge the trailer brakes and open the emergency line shut-off at the rear of the second trailer, there is no air. What does that mean?","Something is wrong and the brakes will not work",["The system is working normally", "The trailer is empty", "The spring brakes are set correctly"],"Check for air at the rear of the second trailer. If air pressure is not there, something is wrong and the brakes will not work.");
F(14,8,"When you charge the trailer brakes and open the emergency line shut-off at the rear of the second trailer, there is no air. What does that mean?","Something is wrong and the brakes will not work. Check for air at the rear of the second trailer. If air pressure is not there, something is wrong and the brakes will not work.");
Q(14,8,2,"What should a visual check of the dolly coupling show?","No space between the upper and lower fifth wheel, and locking jaws closed on the kingpin",["A two-inch gap for turning", "The kingpin resting on top of the jaws", "The safety chains hanging loose"],"Make a visual check of coupling: no space between upper and lower fifth wheel, locking jaws closed on kingpin.");
F(14,8,"What should a visual check of the dolly coupling show?","No space between the upper and lower fifth wheel, and locking jaws closed on the kingpin. Make a visual check of coupling: no space between upper and lower fifth wheel, locking jaws closed on kingpin.");
Q(14,8,2,"When uncoupling a triple-trailer rig, which trailer comes off first?","The third (last) trailer, by pulling the dolly out",["The first trailer", "The middle trailer", "All at once"],"Uncouple the third trailer by pulling the dolly out, then unhitch the dolly; uncouple the rest as you would any double.");
F(14,8,"When uncoupling a triple-trailer rig, which trailer comes off first?","The third (last) trailer, by pulling the dolly out. Uncouple the third trailer by pulling the dolly out, then unhitch the dolly; uncouple the rest as you would any double.");
Q(14,8,2,"Where should you park a set of doubles before uncoupling the rear trailer?","In a straight line on firm, level ground",["On a slope facing downhill", "In a sharp turn", "On soft gravel"],"Park the rig in a straight line on firm level ground and apply the parking brakes so the rig will not move.");
F(14,8,"Where should you park a set of doubles before uncoupling the rear trailer?","In a straight line on firm, level ground. Park the rig in a straight line on firm level ground and apply the parking brakes so the rig will not move.");
Q(14,8,2,"Why do doubles and triples need extra care in bad weather and on slippery roads?","Greater length and more dead axles mean more chance of skids and loss of traction",["They are lighter than single trailers", "Their brakes work better in rain", "They cannot jackknife"],"You have greater length and more dead axles to pull with your drive axles, so there is more chance for skids and loss of traction.");
F(14,8,"Why do doubles and triples need extra care in bad weather and on slippery roads?","Greater length and more dead axles mean more chance of skids and loss of traction. You have greater length and more dead axles to pull with your drive axles, so there is more chance for skids and loss of traction.");
Q(14,8,2,"What should you check before parking a set of doubles or triples in a lot?","That you can pull straight through and will not get stuck",["That the lot has shade", "That the spaces are angled", "That other trucks are nearby"],"Make sure you do not get in a spot you cannot pull straight through. Know how the lot is arranged to avoid a long and difficult escape.");
