Q(14,9,2,"With a tank divided by bulkheads, what must the driver watch when loading and unloading?","Weight distribution, so the front or rear is not overloaded",["The color of the liquid", "The outside temperature only", "The radio antenna"],"When loading and unloading the smaller tanks, pay attention to weight distribution. Do not put too much weight on the front or rear of the vehicle.");
F(14,9,"With a tank divided by bulkheads, what must the driver watch when loading and unloading?","Weight distribution, so the front or rear is not overloaded. When loading and unloading the smaller tanks, pay attention to weight distribution. Do not put too much weight on the front or rear of the vehicle.");
Q(14,9,2,"Why are tanks often only partly filled with dense liquids such as some acids?","A full tank may exceed legal weight limits",["Dense liquids cannot surge", "It makes unloading faster", "It keeps the tank cooler"],"A full tank of dense liquid, such as some acids, may exceed legal weight limits, so tanks are often only partially filled with heavy liquids.");
F(14,9,"Why are tanks often only partly filled with dense liquids such as some acids?","A full tank may exceed legal weight limits. A full tank of dense liquid, such as some acids, may exceed legal weight limits, so tanks are often only partially filled with heavy liquids.");
Q(14,9,2,"How do you control surge when coming to a stop in a tanker?","Keep steady pressure on the brakes and do not release too soon",["Pump the brakes hard and fast", "Release the brakes just before stopping", "Shift to neutral and coast"],"Keep a steady pressure on the brakes. Do not release too soon when coming to a stop. Brake far in advance and increase following distance.");
