Q(14,9,2,"If you must make a quick stop in a tanker to avoid a crash, which braking should you use?","Controlled or stab braking",["Locking the wheels and holding", "The parking brake", "No braking, only steering"],"If you must make a quick stop to avoid a crash, use controlled or stab braking.");
F(14,9,"If you must make a quick stop in a tanker to avoid a crash, which braking should you use?","Controlled or stab braking. If you must make a quick stop to avoid a crash, use controlled or stab braking.");
Q(14,9,2,"What can happen if you steer quickly while braking in a tank vehicle?","The vehicle may roll over",["The brakes cool faster", "The surge stops", "Nothing unusual"],"If you steer quickly while braking, your vehicle may roll over.");
F(14,9,"What can happen if you steer quickly while braking in a tank vehicle?","The vehicle may roll over. If you steer quickly while braking, your vehicle may roll over.");
Q(14,9,2,"How should a tanker take a curve?","Slow down before the curve, then accelerate slightly through it",["Brake hard in the middle of the curve", "Speed up before the curve", "Coast in neutral"],"Slow down before curves, then accelerate slightly through the curve. The posted speed may be too fast for a tank vehicle.");
F(14,9,"How should a tanker take a curve?","Slow down before the curve, then accelerate slightly through it. Slow down before curves, then accelerate slightly through the curve. The posted speed may be too fast for a tank vehicle.");
Q(14,9,2,"How do wet roads change stopping distance?","They double the normal stopping distance",["They cut it in half", "They do not change it", "They add exactly 10 feet"],"Remember that wet roads double the normal stopping distance.");
